    <p class="title is-5 mathjax">
      
        AccurateRAG: A Framework for Building Accurate <span class="search-hit mathjax">Retrieval</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">Augmented</span> Question-Answering Applications
      
    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Nguyen%2C+L+T">Linh The Nguyen</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Tran%2C+C">Chi Tran</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Nguyen%2C+D+N">Dung Ngoc Nguyen</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Pham%2C+V">Van-Cuong Pham</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Ngo%2C+H">Hoang Ngo</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Nguyen%2C+D+Q">Dat Quoc Nguyen</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.02243v2-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        We introduce AccurateRAG -- a novel framework for constructing high-performance question-answering applications based on <span class="search-hit mathjax">retrieval</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">augmented</span> generation (RAG). Our framework offers a pipeline for development efficiency with tools for raw dataset processing, fine-tuning data generation, text embedding &amp; LLM fine-tuni&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.02243v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.02243v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.02243v2-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        We introduce AccurateRAG -- a novel framework for constructing high-performance question-answering applications based on <span class="search-hit mathjax">retrieval</span>-<span class="search-hit mathjax">augmented</span> generation (RAG). Our framework offers a pipeline for development efficiency with tools for raw dataset processing, fine-tuning data generation, text embedding &amp; LLM fine-tuning, output evaluation, and building RAG systems locally. Experimental results show that our framework outperforms previous strong baselines and obtains new state-of-the-art question-answering performance on benchmark datasets.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.02243v2-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.02243v2-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

